  "question": {
    "text": "A force of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> acts on a charged particle placed between two plates of a charged capacitor. If one plate of capacitor is removed, then the force acting on that particle will be."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "Zero",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0073_da4c33a819d9.png\" style=\"width: 146px; height: 140px;\" /></p><p>Electric field due to each plate,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#963;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>Q</mi></mstyle><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Net electric field between the plates,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>net</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p>Force on charged particle between the plates,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0073_bfe22e9711ad.png\" style=\"width: 140px; height: 167px;\" /></p><p>Now, in second case, the net electric field,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#963;</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p>Force on charged particle,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
